      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newtonsville%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office has operated in Newtonsville since 1847, serving the community for over a century and a half.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newtonsville%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1800s, Newtonsville housed a gristmill and a chair factory, fueling local industry in the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newtonsville%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2016, the Ohio State Auditor declared Newtonsville in fiscal caution after discovering poor bookkeeping practices.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newtonsville%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Residents voted to dissolve Newtonsville as a village in November 2019, returning it to Wayne Township after 181 years of incorporation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newtonsville%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The village’s gradual business decline after World War I set the stage for its eventual dissolution in 2019.",
